PAIRING_PARAMETERS|PAIRING_PARAMETERS|Pairing parameters||||Pairing process management
CFG_BONDING_MODE|CFG_BONDING_MODE|Pairing parameters||||Define Bonding modes Possible values: - No-bonding mode(0x00) - Bonding mode(0x01)
CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MAX|CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MAX|Pairing parameters||=CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MIN|16|Encryption key maximum size
CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MIN|CFG_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SIZE_MIN|Pairing parameters||7|16|Encryption key minimum size
CFG_IDENTITY_ADDRESS_TYPE|CFG_IDENTITY_ADDRESS_TYPE|Pairing parameters||||Identity address type Possible values: - Public Identity Address(0x00) - Random Identity Address(0x01)
CFG_IO_CAPABILITY|CFG_IO_CAPABILITY|Application parameters||||Define IO capabilities Possible values: - CFG_IO_CAPABILITY_DISPLAY_ONLY (0x00) - CFG_IO_CAPABILITY_DISPLAY_YES_NO (0x01) - CFG_IO_CAPABILITY_KEYBOARD_ONLY (0x02) - CFG_IO_CAPABILITY_NO_INPUT_NO_OUTPUT (0x03) - CFG_IO_CAPABILITY_KEYBOARD_DISPLAY (0x04)
CFG_MITM_PROTECTION|CFG_MITM_PROTECTION|Application parameters||||Activate/deactivate Define Man In The Middle(MITM) protection mode Possible values: - MITM protection not required (0x00) - MITM protection required (0x01)
CFG_SC_SUPPORT|CFG_SC_SUPPORT|Pairing parameters||||Define Secure Connections Support Possible values: - Secure Connections Paring not supported (0x00) - Secure Connections Paring supported but optional (0x01) - Secure Connections Paring supported and mandatory(0x02)
CFG_KEYPRESS_NOTIFICATION_SUPPORT|CFG_KEYPRESS_NOTIFICATION_SUPPORT|Pairing parameters||||Define MITM modes Possible values: - Keypress notification not supported (0x00) - Keypress notification supported (0x01)
CFG_BLE_IR|CFG_BLE_IR|Pairing parameters||||Identity root key used to derive IRK and DHK(Legacy)
CFG_BLE_IR_HEX|CFG_BLE_IR_HEX|Pairing parameters||||Identity root key used to derive LTK and CSRK
CFG_BLE_ER|CFG_BLE_ER|Pairing parameters||||Encryption root key used to derive LTK(Legacy) and CSRK
CFG_BLE_ER_HEX|CFG_BLE_ER_HEX|BLE Pairing||||Encryption root key used to derive LTK and CSRK
P2P_SERVER_NUMBER|P2P_SERVER_NUMBER|P2P Service||||P2P Server number
L2CAP_REQUEST_NEW_CONN_PARAM|L2CAP_REQUEST_NEW_CONN_PARAM|Application parameters||||L2CAP Connection Update request parameters used for test only with smart Phone
CFG_DEBUG_TRACE_UART|CFG_DEBUG_TRACE_UART|Application parameters||||Enable Debug Trace
CFG_CLI_UART|CFG_CLI_UART|Application parameters||||<font color="red">UART shall be selected when Thread_Cli_Cmd is selected</font>
CFG_UART_GUI|CFG_UART_GUI|Application parameters||||<font color="red">UART shall be selected as it is mandatory for Transparent Mode</font>
CFG_CONSOLE_MENU|CFG_CONSOLE_MENU|Application parameters||||UART choice for GUI
CFG_USB_INTERFACE_ENABLE|CFG_USB_INTERFACE_ENABLE|Application parameters||||Enable/Disable USB interface. Mandatory to be set to Enabled for Transparent Mode VCP
CFG_RTCCLK_DIVIDER_CONF|CFG_RTCCLK_DIVIDER_CONF|Application parameters||||CFG_RTCCLK_DIVIDER_CONF: - Shall be set to either 0,2,4,8,16 - When set to 0, the user sets its own configuration - When set to either 2,4,8,16, the 1Hhz calendar is supported and values of: CFG_RTCCLK_DIV CFG_RTC_WUCKSEL_DIVIDER CFG_RTC_ASYNCH_PRESCALER CFG_RTC_SYNCH_PRESCALER are hard coded in FW
CFG_RTCCLK_DIV|CFG_RTCCLK_DIV|Application parameters||||Accessible only when CFG_RTCCLK_DIVIDER_CONF=0, else it 's hard coded in FW Either 2,4,8,16 RTC Clock Divider
CFG_RTC_WUCKSEL_DIVIDER|CFG_RTC_WUCKSEL_DIVIDER|Application parameters||||Accessible only when CFG_RTCCLK_DIVIDER_CONF=0, else it 's hard coded in FW = 0 when CFG_RTCCLK_DIV = 16 = 1 when CFG_RTCCLK_DIV = 8 = 2 when CFG_RTCCLK_DIV = 4 = 3 when CFG_RTCCLK_DIV = 2
CFG_RTC_ASYNCH_PRESCALER|CFG_RTC_ASYNCH_PRESCALER|Application parameters||0x0|0xFF|Accessible only when CFG_RTCCLK_DIVIDER_CONF=0, else it 's hard coded in FW RTC asynchronous divider Recommended value = CFG_RTCCLK_DIV - 1
CFG_RTC_SYNCH_PRESCALER|CFG_RTC_SYNCH_PRESCALER|Application parameters||0x0|0x7FFF|Accessible only when CFG_RTCCLK_DIVIDER_CONF=0, else it 's hard coded in FW RTC asynchronous divider
OFFSET_PAYLOAD_LENGTH|OFFSET_PAYLOAD_LENGTH|Application parameters||||
OFFSET_PAYLOAD_DATA|OFFSET_PAYLOAD_DATA|Application parameters||||
CFG_BLE_NUM_LINK|CFG_BLE_NUM_LINK|Application parameters||1|8|Maximum number of simultaneous connections that the device will support
CFG_BLE_NUM_GATT_SERVICES|CFG_BLE_NUM_GATT_SERVICES|Application parameters||2||Maximum number of Services that can be stored in the GATT database Maximum value depends on Gatt database size allocated on CPU2 Note that the GAP and GATT services are automatically added so this parameter should be 2 plus the number of user services
CFG_BLE_NUM_GATT_ATTRIBUTES|CFG_BLE_NUM_GATT_ATTRIBUTES|Application parameters||9||Maximum number of Attributes (i.e. the number of characteristic + the number of characteristic values + the number of descriptors, excluding the services) that can be stored in the GATT database. Maximum value depends on Gatt database size allocated on CPU2 Note that certain characteristics and relative descriptors are added automatically during device initialization
CFG_BLE_MAX_ATT_MTU|CFG_BLE_MAX_ATT_MTU|Application parameters||23|512|Maximum supported ATT_MTU size
CFG_BLE_ATT_VALUE_ARRAY_SIZE|CFG_BLE_ATT_VALUE_ARRAY_SIZE|Application parameters||0|65535|Size of the storage area for Attribute values This value depends on the number of attributes used by application. In particular the sum of the following quantities (in octets) should be made for each attribute: - attribute value length - 5, if UUID is 16 bit; 19, if UUID is 128 bit - 2, if server configuration descriptor is used - 2*DTM_NUM_LINK, if client configuration descriptor is used - 2, if extended properties is used The total amount of memory needed is the sum of the above quantities for each attribute. This parameter is ignored by the CPU2 when CFG_BLE_OPTIONS is set to 1
CFG_BLE_DATA_LENGTH_EXTENSION|CFG_BLE_DATA_LENGTH_EXTENSION|Application parameters||||Enable or disable the Extended Packet length feature. Valid values are 0 or 1
CFG_BLE_PERIPHERAL_SCA|CFG_BLE_PERIPHERAL_SCA|Application parameters||||Sleep clock accuracy in Peripheral mode (ppm value)
CFG_BLE_CENTRAL_SCA|CFG_BLE_CENTRAL_SCA|Application parameters||||CFG_BLE_CENTRAL_SCA: Sleep clock accuracy in Central mode 0 : 251 ppm to 500 ppm 1 : 151 ppm to 250 ppm 2 : 101 ppm to 150 ppm 3 : 76 ppm to 100 ppm 4 : 51 ppm to 75 ppm 5 : 31 ppm to 50 ppm 6 : 21 ppm to 30 ppm 7 : 0 ppm to 20 ppm
CFG_BLE_LSE_SOURCE|CFG_BLE_LSE_SOURCE|Application parameters||||Enable or disable the Source for the low speed clock for RF wake-up 1 : external high speed crystal HSE/32/32 0 : external low speed crystal ( no calibration )
CFG_BLE_HSE_STARTUP_TIME|CFG_BLE_HSE_STARTUP_TIME|Application parameters||0x1|0x344|Start up time of the high speed (16 or 32 MHz) crystal oscillator in units of 625/256 us (~2.44 us)
CFG_BLE_MAX_CONN_EVENT_LENGTH|CFG_BLE_MAX_CONN_EVENT_LENGTH|Application parameters||0x0|0xFFFFFFFF|Maximum duration of the connection event when the device is in Slave mode in units of 625/256 us (~2.44 us)
CFG_BLE_VITERBI_MODE|CFG_BLE_VITERBI_MODE|Application parameters||||Enable or disable the Viterbi mode 1 : enabled 0 : disabled
CFG_BLE_OPTIONS|CFG_BLE_OPTIONS|Application parameters||||CFG_BLE_OPTIONS:BLE stack Options flags to be configured with: SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_LL_ONLY SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_LL_HOST SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_NO_SVC_CHANGE_DESC SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_WITH_SVC_CHANGE_DESC SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_DEVICE_NAME_RO SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_DEVICE_NAME_RW SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_EXT_ADV SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_NO_EXT_ADV SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_CS_ALGO2 SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_NO_CS_ALGO2 SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_REDUC_GATTDB_NVM SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_FULL_GATTDB_NVM SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_GATT_CACHING_USED SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_GATT_CACHING_NOTUSED SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_POWER_CLASS_1 SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_POWER_CLASS_2_3 SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_APPEARANCE_WRITABLE SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_APPEARANCE_READONLY SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_ENHANCED_ATT_SUPPORTED SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_ENHANCED_ATT_NOTSUPPORTED *which are used to set following configuration bits: * (bit 0): 1: LL only, 0: LL + host * (bit 1): 1: no service change desc., 0: with service change desc. * (bit 2): 1: device name Read-Only, 0: device name R/W * (bit 3): 1: extended advertizing supported, 0: extended advertizing not supported * (bit 4): 1: CS Algo #2 supported, 0: CS Algo #2 not supported * (bit 5): 1: Reduced GATT database in NVM, 0: Full GATT database in NVM * (bit 6): 1: GATT caching is used, 0: GATT caching is not used * (bit 7): 1: LE Power Class 1, 0: LE Power Class 2-3 * (bit 8): 1: appearance Writable, 0: appearance Read-Only * (bit 9): 1: Enhanced ATT supported, 0: Enhanced ATT not supported * other bits: reserved (shall be set to 0)
CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_LL|- CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_LL|Application parameters||||CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_LL:BLE stack Options flags to be configured with: SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_LL_ONLY SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_LL_HOST * (bit 0): 1: LL only, 0: LL + host
CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_SVC|- CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_SVC|Application parameters||||CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_SVC:BLE stack Options flags to be configured with: SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_NO_SVC_CHANGE_DESC SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_WITH_SVC_CHANGE_DESC * (bit 1): 1: no service change desc., 0: with service change desc.
CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_DEVICE_NAME|- CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_DEVICE_NAME|Application parameters||||CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_DEVICE_NAME:BLE stack Options flags to be configured with: SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_DEVICE_NAME_RO SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_DEVICE_NAME_RW * (bit 2): 1: device name Read-Only, 0: device name R/W
CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_EXT_ADV|- CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_EXT_ADV|Application parameters||||CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_EXT_ADV:BLE stack Options flags to be configured with: SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_EXT_ADV SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_NO_EXT_ADV * (bit 3): 1: extended advertizing supported, 0: extended advertizing not supported
CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_CS_ALGO|- CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_CS_ALGO|Application parameters||||CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_ALGO:BLE stack Options flags to be configured with: SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_CS_ALGO2 SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_NO_CS_ALGO2 * (bit 7): 1: CS Algo #2 supported, 0: CS Algo #2 not supported
CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_GATTDB_NVM|- CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_GATTDB_NVM|Application parameters||||CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_POWER_CLASS:BLE stack Options flags to be configured with: SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_REDUC_GATTDB_NVM SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_FULL_GATTDB_NVM * (bit 5): 1: 1: Reduced GATT database in NVM, 0: Full GATT database in NVM
CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_GATT_CACHING|- CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_GATT_CACHING|Application parameters||||CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_GATT_CACHING:BLE stack Options flags to be configured with: SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_GATT_CACHING_USED SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_GATT_CACHING_NOTUSED * (bit 5): 1: 1: GATT caching is used, 0: GATT caching is not used
CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_POWER_CLASS|- CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_POWER_CLASS|Application parameters||||CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_POWER_CLASS:BLE stack Options flags to be configured with: SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_POWER_CLASS_1 SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_POWER_CLASS_2_3 * (bit 7): 1: LE Power Class 1, 0: LE Power Class 2-3
CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_APPEARANCE|- CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_APPEARANCE|Application parameters||||CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_APPEARANCE:BLE stack Options flags to be configured with: SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_APPEARANCE_WRITABLE SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_APPEARANCE_READONLY * (bit 8): 1: 1: appearance Writable, 0: appearance Read-Only
CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_ENHANCED_ATT|- CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_ENHANCED_ATT|Application parameters||||CFG_BLE_OPTIONS_ENHANCED_ATT:BLE stack Options flags to be configured with: SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_ENHANCED_ATT_SUPPORTED SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_ENHANCED_ATT_NOTSUPPORTED * (bit 9): 1: 1: Enhanced ATT supported, 0: Enhanced ATT not supported
CFG_BLE_MAX_COC_INITIATOR_NBR|CFG_BLE_MAX_COC_INITIATOR_NBR|Application parameters||0|64|Maximum number of connection-oriented channels in initiator mode
CFG_BLE_MIN_TX_POWER|CFG_BLE_MIN_TX_POWER|Application parameters||-127|20|Minimum transmit power in dBm supported by the Controller.
CFG_BLE_MAX_TX_POWER|CFG_BLE_MAX_TX_POWER|Application parameters||=CFG_BLE_MIN_TX_POWER|20|Maximum transmit power in dBm supported by the Controller.
CFG_BLE_MAX_ADD_EATT_BEARERS|CFG_BLE_MAX_ADD_EATT_BEARERS|Application parameters||0|4|BLE stack Maximum number of created Enhanced ATT bearers to be configured in addition to the number of links - Range: 0 __ 4
CFG_BLE_EXTRA_DATA_BUFFER_SIZE|CFG_BLE_EXTRA_DATA_BUFFER_SIZE|Application parameters||0|500|Size of the RAM buffer extra_data_buffer allocated for the extension of Host commands - Range: 0..500 (at least >250)
CFG_BLE_EXTRA_DATA_STATUS|CFG_BLE_EXTRA_DATA_STATUS|Application parameters||||
CFG_BLE_RX_MODEL_CONFIG|CFG_BLE_RX_MODEL_CONFIG|Application parameters||||BLE Rx model configuration flags to be configured with: - SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_RX_MODEL_AGC_RSSI_LEGACY - SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_RX_MODEL_AGC_RSSI_BLOCKER which are used to set following configuration bits: (bit 0): 1: agc_rssi model improved vs RF blockers 0: Legacy agc_rssi model other bits: reserved (shall be set to 0)
CFG_BLE_MAX_ADV_SET_NBR|CFG_BLE_MAX_ADV_SET_NBR|Application parameters||1|8|Maximum number of advertising sets. Range: 1 .. 8 with limitation: This parameter is linked to CFG_BLE_MAX_ADV_DATA_LEN such as both compliant with allocated Total memory computed with BLE_EXT_ADV_BUFFER_SIZE based on Max Extended advertising configuration supported. This parameter is considered by the CPU2 when CFG_BLE_OPTIONS has SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_EXT_ADV flag set
CFG_BLE_MAX_ADV_DATA_LEN|CFG_BLE_MAX_ADV_DATA_LEN|Application parameters||31|1650|Maximum advertising data length (in bytes) Range: 31 .. 1650 with limitation: This parameter is linked to CFG_BLE_MAX_ADV_SET_NBR such as both compliant with allocated Total memory computed with BLE_EXT_ADV_BUFFER_SIZE based on Max Extended advertising configuration supported. This parameter is considered by the CPU2 when CFG_BLE_OPTIONS has SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_OPTIONS_EXT_ADV flag set
CFG_BLE_TX_PATH_COMPENS|CFG_BLE_TX_PATH_COMPENS|Application parameters||-1280|1280|RF TX Path Compensation Value (16-bit signed integer). Units: 0.1 dB. Range: -1280 .. 1280
CFG_BLE_RX_PATH_COMPENS|CFG_BLE_RX_PATH_COMPENS|Application parameters||-1280|1280|RF RX Path Compensation Value (16-bit signed integer). Units: 0.1 dB. Range: -1280 .. 1280
CFG_BLE_CORE_VERSION|CFG_BLE_CORE_VERSION|Application parameters||||BLE core version (16-bit signed integer). - SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_BLE_CORE_5_2 - SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_BLE_CORE_5_3 - SHCI_C2_BLE_INIT_BLE_CORE_5_4 which are used to set: 11(5.2), 12(5.3), 13(5.4).
CFG_TLBLE_EVT_QUEUE_LENGTH|CFG_TLBLE_EVT_QUEUE_LENGTH|Application parameters||1||"Queue length of BLE Event This parameter defines the number of asynchronous events that can be stored in the HCI layer before being reported to the application. When a command is sent to the BLE core coprocessor, the HCI layer is waiting for the event with the Num_HCI_Command_Packets set to 1. The receive queue shall be large enough to store all asynchronous events received in between. When CFG_TLBLE_MOST_EVENT_PAYLOAD_SIZE is set to 27, this allow to store three 255 bytes long asynchronous events between the HCI command and its event. Maximum value depends on SRAM2 size available This parameter depends on the value given to CFG_TLBLE_MOST_EVENT_PAYLOAD_SIZE. When the queue size is to small, the system may hang if the queue is full with asynchronous events and the HCI layer is still waiting for a CC/CS event, In that case, the notification TL_BLE_HCI_ToNot() is called to indicate to the application a HCI command did not receive its command event within 30s (Default HCI Timeout)."
CFG_TLBLE_MOST_EVENT_PAYLOAD_SIZE|CFG_TLBLE_MOST_EVENT_PAYLOAD_SIZE|Application parameters||||This parameter should be set to fit most events received by the HCI layer. It defines the buffer size of each element allocated in the queue of received events and can be used to optimize the amount of RAM allocated by the Memory Manager. It should not exceed 255 which is the maximum HCI packet payload size (a greater value is a lost of memory as it will never be used)
DBG_TRACE_USE_CIRCULAR_QUEUE|DBG_TRACE_USE_CIRCULAR_QUEUE|Generic parameters||||When not set, the traces is looping on sending the trace over UART
CFG_HW_RESET_BY_FW|CFG_HW_RESET_BY_FW|Generic parameters||||When set, this resets some hw resources to set the device in the same state than the power up The FW resets only register that may prevent the FW to run properly This shall be set to 0 in a final product
CFG_USE_SMPS|CFG_USE_SMPS|Generic parameters||||When set, this set SMPS supply SMPS not used when Set to 0 SMPS used when Set to 1
CFG_LED_SUPPORTED|CFG_LED_SUPPORTED|Generic parameters||||When set, this resets some hw resources to set the device in the same state than the power up The FW resets only register that may prevent the FW to run properly This shall be set to 0 in a final product
CFG_BUTTON_SUPPORTED|CFG_BUTTON_SUPPORTED|Generic parameters||||When set, this resets some hw resources to set the device in the same state than the power up The FW resets only register that may prevent the FW to run properly This shall be set to 0 in a final product
CFG_DEBUG_BLE_TRACE|CFG_DEBUG_BLE_TRACE|Generic parameters||||Enable or disable traces in the BLE services
CFG_DEBUG_APP_TRACE|CFG_DEBUG_APP_TRACE|Generic parameters||||Enable or disable traces in application
CFG_FULL_LOW_POWER|CFG_FULL_LOW_POWER|Generic parameters||||Enable or disable light traces in the THREAD and ZIGBEE services. CFG_HW_USART1_ENABLED and or CFG_HW_LPUART1_ENABLED must be set as well as CFG_DEBUG_TRACE_UART. In Zigbee applications, it forces the network mode to Centralized and the device role to Sleepy End Device, and a Sleepy End Device has to enable this full low power parameter.
CFG_LPM_SUPPORTED|CFG_LPM_SUPPORTED|Generic parameters||||Low Power mode: When set to 1, the low power mode is Enable When set to 0, the device stays in RUN mode
CFG_LPM_STANDBY_SUPPORTED|CFG_LPM_STANDBY_SUPPORTED|Generic parameters||||Low Power Standby mode: This shall be set to 1 when standby is supported while the wireless stack on CPU2 is running(i.e the CPU2 is allowed to enter standby between RF activity) * Otherwise, it should be set to 0 for marginal code and test execution saving * In this case the lowest power mode available will be Stop 1 * Note that keeping that setting to 1 when standby is not supported does not hurt
CFG_DEBUGGER_SUPPORTED|CFG_DEBUGGER_SUPPORTED|Generic parameters||||Enable or disable debugger, default value set to 1
CFG_DEBUG_TRACE|CFG_DEBUG_TRACE|Generic parameters||||Enable or disable traces in the THREAD and Zigbee services
CFG_DEBUG_TRACE_LIGHT|CFG_DEBUG_TRACE_LIGHT|Generic parameters||||Enable or disable light traces
CFG_DEBUG_TRACE_FULL|CFG_DEBUG_TRACE_FULL|Generic parameters||||Enable or disable full traces
DBG_TRACE_MSG_QUEUE_SIZE|DBG_TRACE_MSG_QUEUE_SIZE|Generic parameters||=MAX_DBG_TRACE_MSG_SIZE||Max buffer Size to queue data traces and max data trace allowed. Only Used if DBG_TRACE_USE_CIRCULAR_QUEUE is defined Min value is MAX_DBG_TRACE_MSG_SIZE value Max value depends on SRAM size available
MAX_DBG_TRACE_MSG_SIZE|MAX_DBG_TRACE_MSG_SIZE|Generic parameters||1||Max value depends on SRAM size available
BLE_CFG_PERIPHERAL|The device needs to support the Peripheral Role|BLE Services Configuration||||This setting shall be set to '1' if the device needs to support the Peripheral Role. In the MS configuration, both BLE_CFG_PERIPHERAL and BLE_CFG_CENTRAL shall be set to '1
BLE_CFG_CENTRAL|The device needs to support the Central Role|BLE Services Configuration||||This setting shall be set to '1' if the device needs to support the Central Role. In the MS configuration, both BLE_CFG_PERIPHERAL and BLE_CFG_CENTRAL shall be set to '1
