BLE_ADDR_TYPE|Address Type|Advertising configuration||||List of advertising types, can be: --> <!-- - Public address(PUBLIC_ADDR 0) --> <!-- - Random address (RANDOM_ADDR 1); if you activate RNG then you will get the choice between STATIC and DYNAMIC Random address
CFG_STATIC_RANDOM_ADDRESS|RANDOM_ADDRESS type|Advertising configuration||||List of random address types, can be: - Static, Random Address is fixed for lifetime of the device - Dynamic, Random Address is generated with the RNG at each bootup.
STATIC_RANDOM_ADDRESS|STATIC_RANDOM_ADDRESS|Advertising configuration||0x000000000000|0xFFFFFFFFFFFF|ex: 0xf257acd87a6c
CFG_STATIC_UNIQUE_RANDOM_ADDR_LSB|CFG_STATIC_UNIQUE_RANDOM_ADDR_LSB|Advertising configuration||0x0000|0xFFFF|
CFG_RNG|RNG status|Advertising configuration||||
ADV_FILTER|Advertising Filter|Advertising configuration||||Advertising policy for filtering (white list related), can be: - Process scan and connection requests from all devices, i.e. the White List is not in use.(NO_WHITE_LIST_USE 0x00) - Process connection requests from all devices and only scan requests from devices that are in the White List.(WHITE_LIST_FOR_ONLY_SCAN 0x01) - Process scan requests from all devices and only connection requests from devices that are in the White List (WHITE_LIST_FOR_ONLY_CONN 0x02) - Process scan and connection requests only from devices in the White List.(WHITE_LIST_FOR_ALL 0x03)
