THREAD|THREAD|THREAD application type||||
THREAD_APPLICATION|Thread Application|THREAD application type||||List of applications types, can be: - Full Thread Device with Command Line Interface(FTD_CLI) - Thread_Coap_GenericFull Thread Device with network configuration(FTD) - Minimal Thread Device with network configuration(MTD)
PANID|PANID|Parameters||||Personal Area Network Identifier (PAN ID): an unsigned 16-bit value that specifies the PAN ID. <font color="E6007E"><b>WARNING!: </b></font>The PAN ID MUST be different from 0xFFFF value which is reserved for broadcast PAN ID <b>Value range : </b>0x0 to 0xFFFE
CHANNEL|CHANNEL|Parameters||11|26|2.4 GHz channel as defined in Section 6.1.2.1 of [IEEE802154]
NETWORKKEY|NETWORKKEY|Parameters||||Thread network key
APP_DBG_EN|APP_DBG_EN|Application parameters||||Enable or Disable traces in application
APPLI_CONFIG_LOG_LEVEL|APPLI_CONFIG_LOG_LEVEL|Application parameters||||List of Log level for Application, can be: - LOG_LEVEL_NONE (None) - LOG_LEVEL_CRIT (Critical) - LOG_LEVEL_WARN (Warning) - LOG_LEVEL_INFO (Info) - LOG_LEVEL_DEBG (Debug)
APPLI_PRINT_FILE_FUNC_LINE|APPLI_PRINT_FILE_FUNC_LINEs|Application parameters||||
CFG_TL_EVT_QUEUE_LENGTH|CFG_TL_EVT_QUEUE_LENGTH|Application parameters||||Queue length of BLE Event This parameter defines the number of asynchronous events that can be stored in the HCI layer before being reported to the application. When a command is sent to the BLE core coprocessor, the HCI layer is waiting for the event with the Num_HCI_Command_Packets set to 1. The receive queue shall be large enough to store all asynchronous events received in between. When CFG_TL_MOST_EVENT_PAYLOAD_SIZE is set to 27, this allow to store three 255 bytes long asynchronous events between the HCI command and its event. This parameter depends on the value given to CFG_TL_MOST_EVENT_PAYLOAD_SIZE. When the queue size is to small, the system may hang if the queue is full with asynchronous events and the HCI layer is still waiting for a CC/CS event, In that case, the notification TL_BLE_HCI_ToNot() is called to indicate to the application a HCI command did not receive its command event within 30s (Default HCI Timeout).
CFG_TL_MOST_EVENT_PAYLOAD_SIZE|CFG_TL_MOST_EVENT_PAYLOAD_SIZE|Application parameters||4|255|This parameter should be set to fit most events received by the HCI layer. It defines the buffer size of each element allocated in the queue of received events and can be used to optimize the amount of RAM allocated by the Memory Manager. It should not exceed 255 which is the maximum HCI packet payload size (a greater value is a lost of memory as it will never be used) It shall be at least 4 to receive the command status event in one frame. The default value is set to 27 to allow receiving an event of MTU size in a single buffer. This value maybe reduced * further depending on the application.
ZIGBEE|ZIGBEE|ZIGBEE application type||||
ZGB_APPLICATION|Zigbee Application|ZIGBEE application type||||List of Zigbee application type, can be: - Full Function Device (FFD) - Reduced Function Device with only End Device and Sleepy End Device available for lower energy consumption(RFD)
ZGB_NW_MODE|Zigbee Network Mode|ZIGBEE application type||||Network configuration, can be: - Centralized - Distributed - Touchlink
ZGB_DEVICE_ROLE|Zigbee Device Role|ZIGBEE application type||||List of application type, can be: - Coordinator (for FFD application only) - Router (for FFD application only) - End Device - Sleepy End Device
ZGB_TOUCHLINK_CAPABILITY|Touchlink capability|ZIGBEE application type||||Touchlink device can handle 2 capabilities in RFD application: - Router - End device, which allows Sleepy mode
ZGB_SLEEPY_MODE|Sleepy mode|ZIGBEE application type||||Sleepy mode is available in RFD applications, except in Touchlink mode for router capability. It turns on the low power mode parameters.
ZGB_NB_ENDPOINTS|Number of End Points|End Points||1|10|Number of endpoints used on one device. At least one endpoint is mandatory for a Zigbee application, and it should not exceed 10.
ZGB_CHANNEL|Channel|Network Parameters||0|26|Network channel should be set between 0 and 26.
ENDPOINT1_ID_ZGB|Endpoint ID|Endpoint||1|240|Endpoint <b>242</b> shall be reserved for the <b>Green Power cluster</b>, used in proxy mode with FFD application and not used with RFD application. <font color="E6007E"><b>WARNING:</b> Endpoint IDs shall be <b>unique</b> in one same device.
ENDPOINT1_ID|Endpoint ID|Endpoint||1|240|Endpoint <b>242</b> shall be reserved for the <b>Green Power cluster</b>, used in proxy mode with FFD application and not used with RFD application. <font color="E6007E"><b>WARNING:</b> Endpoint IDs shall be <b>unique</b> in one same device.
ZGB_ENDPOINT1_PROFILE_ID|Profile ID|Endpoint||||Profile of the endpoint, can be: - Home Automation (HA) - Smart Energy (SE) - Zigbee Light Link (ZLL)
ENDPOINT1_DEVICE_ID|Device ID|Endpoint||||Device description gives a readable information about the application of the device
ZCL_BASIC_ENDPOINT1|Basic|Clusters||||Basic cluster: server mode mandatory for all Zigbee endpoint.
ZCL_IDENTIFY_ENDPOINT1|Identify|Clusters||||Identify cluster allows to be in identification mode. - Server receives commands to start and stop identification mode. - Client sends start and stop commands to the server.
ZCL_ALARM_ENDPOINT1|Alarms|Clusters||||Alarm cluster configure alarm functionality and send alarm notifications. - Server resides with other clusters which can generate alarm conditions and it sends them to a cluster client. Time server cluster SHALL be set when Alarms server is used. - Client can send user instructions to the server.
ZCL_TIME_ENDPOINT1|Time|Clusters||||Time cluster provides a base for real-time application. - Server acts as a time master for the network. It SHALL be set when Alarm server or DRLC client are used. - Client synchronizes itself with the server.
ZCL_COMMISSIONING_ENDPOINT1|Commissioning|Clusters||||Commissioning cluster allows a commissioning process. - Server responds to a commissioning process and commissions itself into a network. - Client initiates the commissioning of a commissioning server.
ZCL_GROUPS_ENDPOINT1|Groups|Clusters||||Groups cluster manages group addressing. - Server receives configuration commands regarding to the local group table. - Client sends commands to configure the group table.
ZCL_SCENES_ENDPOINT1|Scenes|Clusters||||Scenes cluster allows to configure a set of stored values to create recalling scenes. - Server receives commands to configure scenes. - Client controls the configuration of the scenes.
ZCL_OCCUPANCY_SENSING_ENDPOINT1|Occupancy Sensing|Clusters||||Occupancy Sensing cluster provides an interface to an occupancy sensor. - Server receives commands to configure the sensor and reports to the client. - Client sends commands to configure the sensor and receives report from the sensor.
ZCL_DIAGNOSTICS_ENDPOINT1|Diagnostics|Clusters||||Diagnostic cluster informs about the operation of the stack over time and will be used by multiple profiles. As a result it should not be set alone. - Server provides diagnostic data. Attributes are strongly recommended to be stored in persistent memory. - Client sends requests to access diagnostic data.
ZCL_POLL_CONTROL_ENDPOINT1|Poll Control|Clusters||||Poll Control cluster provides a mechanism for the management of a Zigbee End Device's polling mode.It defines the poll interval between (normal or fast) two MAC Data Requests from the ZED to its parent router. - Server sets the polling mode to Normal (long poll interval) or Fast (short poll interval) after periodically checking the client. - Client decides the polling mode to be selected.
ZCL_POWER_CONFIGURATION_ENDPOINT1|Power Configuration|Clusters||||Power Configuration cluster provides information about the power source and voltage alarms to be configured. - Server receives commands to set its power configuration. - Client sends commands to set the power configuration on a remote device.
ZCL_POWER_PROFILE_ENDPOINT1|Power Profile|Clusters||||Power Profile cluster indicates the expected power profile to a controller. - Server provides the local power profile. - Client receives the power profile.
ZCL_RSSI_LOCATION_ENDPOINT1|RSSI Location|Clusters||||RSSI Location cluster allows exchanges of Received Signal Strength Indication information. - Server requests RSSI information and report RSSI measurement. - Client answers to the server requests and reports.
ZCL_PRESSURE_MEASUREMENT_ENDPOINT1|Pressure Measurement|Clusters||||Pressure Measurement cluster provides an interface to configure and control pressure measurement. - Server measures the pressure. - Client configures the server and receives measurements from it.
ZCL_DEVICE_TEMPERATURE_CONFIGURATION_ENDPOINT1|Device Temperature Configuration|Clusters||||Device Temperature Configuration cluster measures internal temperature and configures temperature alarms. - Server receives commands to access internal temperature data. - Client sends commands to access the internal temperature.
ZCL_TEMPERATURE_MEASUREMENT_ENDPOINT1|Temperature Measurement|Clusters||||Temperature Measurement cluster provides an interface to configure and control temperature measurements. - Server measures the temperature. - Client configures the server and receives measurements from it.
ZCL_THERMOSTAT_ENDPOINT1|Thermostat Configuration|Clusters||||Thermostat cluster provides an interface to configure and control a thermostat. - Server configures the thermostat. - Client controls the functionalities of the thermostat.
ZCL_THERMOSTAT_UI_CONFIGURATION_ENDPOINT1|Thermostat User Interface Configuration|Clusters||||Thermostat UI Configuration cluster provides an interface to configure the user interface of a thermostat. - Server configures the thermostat UI. - Client controls the functionalities of the thermostat UI.
ZCL_METER_IDENTIFICATION_ENDPOINT1|Meter Identification|Clusters||||Meter Identification cluster determines advanced information about utility metering device. - Server provides information. - Client sends requests to the server for information.
ZCL_ELECTRICALMEASUREMENT_ENDPOINT1|Electrical Measurement|Clusters||||Electrical Measurement cluster provides an interface to configure and control electrical measurements. - Server makes the electrical measurements. - Client configures the server and receives measurements from it.
ZCL_FAN_CONTROL_ENDPOINT1|Fan Control|Clusters||||Fan Control cluster controls the speed and state of a fan. - Server configures the speed or state of the fan. - Client commands the server to set the speed or state of the fan.
ZCL_PUMP_CONFIGURATION_CONTROL_ENDPOINT1|Pump Configuration and Control|Clusters||||Pump Configuration and Control cluster provides an interface to configure and control pump devices (control of speed not included). - Server configures the pump. - Client controls the functionalities of the pump.
ZCL_WATER_CONTENT_MEASUREMENT_ENDPOINT1|Water Content Measurement|Clusters||||Water Content Measurement cluster provides an interface to configure and control humidity measurements. - Server measures the humidity. - Client configures the server and receives measurements from it.
ZCL_ONOFF_ENDPOINT1|On/Off|Clusters||||On/Off cluster provides functionality to switch a device between On and Off states. - Server receives commands to change the state. Server mode SHALL be set if Level Control cluster OR if Color Control are in server mode. - Client sends commands to request a change of state.
ZCL_COLORCONTROL_ENDPOINT1|Color Control|Clusters||||Color Control cluster controls the color of a light. - Server receives commands to change the color of the light. - Client sends commands to change the color of the remote light.
ZCL_ILLUMINANCE_LEVEL_SENSING_ENDPOINT1|Illuminance Level Sensing|Clusters||||Illuminance Level Sensing cluster provides an interface to configure and control level of illumination watch. - Server senses the level of illumination. - Client configures and gets the notifications from the server.
ZCL_ILLUMINANCE_MEASUREMENT_ENDPOINT1|Illuminance Measurement|Clusters||||Illuminance Measurement cluster provides an interface to configure and control illuminance measurements. - Server measures the illuminance and report to the client. - Client configures the server and control receives measurements from it.
ZCL_LEVELCONTROL_ENDPOINT1|Level Control|Clusters||||Level Control cluster controls the level of a characteristic value of a device. - Server receives commands to change the level of characteristic values. OnOff server SHALL be set when Level Control server is used. - Client sends commands to change the level of characteristic values.
ZCL_ON_OFF_SWITCH_CONFIGURATION_ENDPOINT1|On/Off Switch Configuration|Clusters||||On/Off Switch Configuration cluster provides the switch type on a device. - Server receives commands to define a switch configuration. - Client sends commands to define a switch configuration.
ZCL_DOOR_LOCK_ENDPOINT1|Door Lock|Clusters||||Door Lock cluster provides an interface to configure and control generic values of door locks and doors. - Server sets the values representing door security. - Client controls the door lock and the door.
ZCL_WINDOW_COVERING_ENDPOINT1|Window Covering|Clusters||||Window Covering cluster provides an interface to configure and control window coverings. - Server sets the values of the window covering. - Client controls the window covering.
ZCL_IAS_ACE_ENDPOINT1|IAS Ancillary Control Equipment (ACE)|Clusters||||IAS ACE cluster provides an interface to configure and control a Control and Indicating Equipment (CIE) in an Intruder Alarm System (IAS). - Server receives commands to configure the CIE. - Client sends commands to configure and control the CIE.
ZCL_IAS_WD_ENDPOINT1|IAS Warning Device (WD)|Clusters||||IAS WD cluster provides an interface to configure and control a Warning Device (WD) in an Intruder Alarm System (IAS). - Server receives commands to configure the WD and report to the client. - Client sends commands to configure and control the WD and receives reports.
ZCL_IAS_ZONE_ENDPOINT1|IAS Zone|Clusters||||IAS Zone cluster provides an interface to configure and control an IAS security zone device. - Server receives commands to configure the IAS Zone device and report to the client. - Client sends commands to configure and control the IAS Zone device and receives reports.
ZCL_MESSAGING_ENDPOINT1|Messaging|Clusters||||Messaging cluster an interface to pass text messages from one device to another. - Server sends the text message. - Client receives the text message.
ZCL_DRLC_ENDPOINT1|Demand Response and Load Control|Clusters||||DRLC cluster provides an interface to the functionality of Demand Response and Load Control. - Server sends the Load Control Events to the devices. - Client receives the Load Control Events. It is time-dependent, therefore a Time server cluster SHALL be set when DRLC client is used.
ZCL_METERING_ENDPOINT1|Metering|Clusters||||Metering cluster provides an interface to obtain usage information from metering devices. - Server gives information. - Client asks for usage information to the server.
ZCL_PRICE_ENDPOINT1|Price|Clusters||||Price cluster provides an interface to communicates pricing information. - Server gives price information. - Client asks for price information to the server.
ZCL_TUNNELING_ENDPOINT1|Smart Energy Tunneling|Clusters||||Smart Energy Tunneling cluster provides an interface for tunneling protocols. - Server provides and manages tunnels. - Client requests a tunnel and close it.
ZCL_KEY_ESTABLISHMENT_ENDPOINT1|Key Establishment|Clusters||||Key Establishment cluster is to be used for communication between devices if original network security can not be trusted. - Server initiates the secure communication transaction. - Client responds the secure communication transation.
ZCL_DEHUMIDIFICATION_CONTROL_ENDPOINT1|Dehumidification Control|Clusters||||Dehumidification Control cluster provides an interface to configure an control dehumidification devices. - Server configures the dehumidification device. - Client controls the functionalities of the dehumidification device.
ZCL_BALLAST_CONFIGURATION_ENDPOINT1|Ballast Configuration|Clusters||||Ballast Configuration cluster provides an interface to configure an control lighting ballasts. - Server receives command to configure the lighting ballasts. - Client sends commands to configure and control lighting ballasts.
ZCL_NEAREST_GATEWAY_ENDPOINT1|Nearest Gateway|Clusters||||Nearest Gateway cluster provides an interface to send nearest gateway information. - Server gives the information of nearest gateway. - Client asks for the nearest gateway.
ZCL_OTA_UPGRADE_ENDPOINT1|OTA Upgrade|Specific Clusters||||OTA Upgrade cluster allows to upgrade application software over the air. - Server distributes the software to upgrade. - Client receives the software to update.
ZCL_VOICE_OVER_ZGB_ENDPOINT1|Voice Over Zigbee|Specific Clusters||||Voice Over Zigbee cluster allows voice transmition between Zigbee devices. - Server receives the voice message. - Client sends the voice message.
